# Mirror of docs/team/ownership.md. GitHub routes PR reviews to these owners; branch protection needs one
# approving review from a code owner of every file touched. Every path has an owner and a backup, so the
# backup approves the owner's own PRs and nobody waits for the lead. The lead (Faizan) is required only for
# platform core, packages, docs/architecture and the team rules; module contracts belong to the module owner.
# Himanshu is the third owner of the host, tests, infra and CI paths: the branch rule refuses an approval from the
# person who made the last push, and the merge queue pushes updates from Faizan's account, so Srujan's PRs there
# need an approver who is neither Srujan nor Faizan.
# Until the v1.0 launch (target Thu 12 Nov 2026, lead's decision of 5 Nov), Faizan is also an owner of every
# module path, so the automated review's approval on his behalf (auto-review.yml, auto-approve.yml) counts as the
# code-owner approval for module code. The module owners still review, after the merge if not before. A PR opened
# from Faizan's account (Claude builds) still needs one of the other owners. Remove the @faizanrooman entries on
# /modules/ lines after the launch.

